WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.175
What's New in

00:00:00.987 --> 00:00:02.625
PHP 8.6

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:04.741
PHP 8.6 is

00:00:04.553 --> 00:00:05.048
out

00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:05.956
with the release

00:00:05.768 --> 00:00:06.935
notes covering what's

00:00:06.747 --> 00:00:07.312
new in the

00:00:07.124 --> 00:00:07.878
release

00:00:08.398 --> 00:00:09.647
Its representation

00:00:09.459 --> 00:00:10.461
is independent of

00:00:10.356 --> 00:00:11.216
any time and

00:00:11.028 --> 00:00:12.336
timezone and can

00:00:12.148 --> 00:00:13.162
represent a range

00:00:12.973 --> 00:00:13.740
of more than

00:00:13.551 --> 00:00:15.992
250 years with nanosecond

00:00:15.804 --> 00:00:16.570
precision

00:00:17.102 --> 00:00:18.918
PHP 8.6 is

00:00:18.729 --> 00:00:19.802
a major update

00:00:19.614 --> 00:00:20.498
of the PHP

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:20.993
language

00:00:21.147 --> 00:00:22.278
with new features

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.587
including Partial Function

00:00:23.399 --> 00:00:24.271
Application

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:25.510
a new Duration

00:00:25.321 --> 00:00:25.899
class

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.278
a Polling API

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.104
and a new

00:00:27.916 --> 00:00:28.929
clamp function

00:00:29.454 --> 00:00:30.468
Full story on

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:31.175
the dashboard
